 "persona_full": "[Who I am]\n- I am a man.\n- I am 37 years old.\n- I live in Kerala.\n- The place I live in has 10,000-20,000 inhabitants.\n- I am Hindu.\n- I am married.\n- I have 2 children.\n- I live with my parents.\n- My education: complete secondary school (university-preparatory).\n- I can read and write.\n\n[Work and money]\n- My work situation: full-time employee.\n- I am the chief wage earner in my household.\n- I would describe my family as lower middle class.\n- On a ladder of household incomes in India from 1 (lowest) to 10 (highest), my household is at 4.\n- In the past year my family saved money.\n- My satisfaction with my household's financial situation, from 1 (completely dissatisfied) to 10 (completely satisfied): 8.\n- In the last 12 months my family has never gone without enough food to eat.\n- In the last 12 months my family has sometimes gone without a cash income.\n\n[My life]\n- Taking all things together, I am very happy.\n- My health these days is poor.\n- My satisfaction with my life as a whole, from 1 (completely dissatisfied) to 10 (completely satisfied): 9.\n- How much free choice and control I feel I have over my life, from 1 (none at all) to 10 (a great deal): 9.\n- In my neighbourhood I feel very secure.\n- Family is very important in my life.\n- Friends are very important in my life.\n- Work is very important in my life.\n- Politics is rather important in my life.\n- Religion is not very important in my life.\n\n[Religion]\n- Apart from weddings and funerals, I attend religious services once a week.\n- How important God is in my life, from 1 (not at all important) to 10 (very important): 8.\n\n[How I see other people]\n- My family: I trust them somewhat.\n- People in my neighbourhood: I trust them somewhat.\n- People I know personally: I trust them somewhat.\n\n[What kind of person I am]\n- Thinking up new ideas and being creative, doing things my own way: very much like me.\n- Being rich, having a lot of money and expensive things: somewhat like me.\n- Living in secure surroundings, avoiding anything that might be dangerous: very much like me.\n- Always behaving properly, avoiding anything people would say is wrong: somewhat like me.\n- Tradition, following the customs handed down by my religion or family: not like me.\n\n[My views]\n- I am somewhat interested in politics.\n- From 1 (incomes should be made more equal) to 10 (we need larger income differences as incentives for individual effort), my view is 3.\n- From 1 (competition is good) to 10 (competition is harmful), my view is 7.\n- Cheating on taxes if you have a chance, from 1 (never justifiable) to 10 (always justifiable): 1.\n- I am very proud to be Indian.\n\n[How I get information]\n- How often I read a daily newspaper: daily.\n- How often I watch TV news: daily.\n- How often I use the internet: monthly.",
